---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy & Terms — GPUCalc"
  description="GPUCalc is a client-side calculator designed with zero telemetry and total user privacy."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8 py-4 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-slate-800 pb-6 space-y-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy & Terms of Use
      </h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400">Last updated: February 2026</p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">1. Client-Side Execution & Zero Telemetry</h2>
      <p>
        GPUCalc operates as a fully client-side single-page architecture and static web application. All calculations, parameter configurations, slider inputs, and model memory estimations are evaluated directly inside your local web browser session using JavaScript.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do <b>not</b> transmit, collect, or store your custom model parameter counts, prompt sequence lengths, or training batch configurations on any external server.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">2. Local Storage Usage</h2>
      <p>
        The only data stored on your local browser is your visual color theme preference (<code class="text-indigo-300">localStorage.getItem('theme')</code>) to ensure consistent dark or light styling across page transitions without screen flashing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">3. Cloud GPU Pricing & Third-Party Outbound Links</h2>
      <p>
        The pricing information presented in the Live GPU Matrix is compiled from public provider documentation and marketplace spot bids. When you click "Rent" or "Deploy", you are redirected to third-party cloud platforms (e.g. RunPod, Lambda Labs, Vast.ai, AWS, Google Cloud).
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not control the terms, pricing fluctuations, or availability guarantees of these external providers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">4. Disclaimer of Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        GPU calculations are mathematical estimates intended for planning and sizing purposes. Real-world CUDA memory consumption may vary slightly depending on PyTorch allocator fragmentation, CUDA driver version, kernel buffer allocations, and specific model quantization implementations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-100">5. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this policy, please reach out via our <a href="/contact" class="text-indigo-400 underline hover:text-indigo-300">Contact & Feedback page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
